WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.260
In America,

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.300
socialism is hot again.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.740
Democratic socialism

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.660
is your kids public school.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.420
It's our interstate highway system.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.920
It's the researchers and scientists

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.200
paid with our taxes.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.280
We can do better

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.500
when we do them together.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.360
Really?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.520
I know better

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.260
because I'm from Guatemala.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.780
I've seen the impact of

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.620
socialism.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.160
My father escaped Cuba.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.300
My grandfather

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.500
suffered under Communists in Hungary

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.020
before escaping.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.020
As a child,

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.180
I was taught socialism was wrong.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.340
I grew up mocking it,

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.520
but democratic socialism sounded okay.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.040
It made sense to me that

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.000
government should take care of the economy.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.460
It's complete anarchy.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.880
But then, I watched socialism fail in Latin America.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.340
I learned that

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.100
every time a country

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.040
started down the socialist path,

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.980
it failed.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.880
When Castro came to power,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.300
people were excited.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.500
They cheered.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.380
He was going to help the poor

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.740
and make everyone equal.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:06.560
But the result?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.780
Sailing for freedom

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.740
aboard an old green Chevy truck.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.680
Hundreds of thousands fled Cuba.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.400
Here, in Little Havana in Miami,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.440
Cubans who escaped are eager to remind people

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.280
how bad life in Cuba had become.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.020
This man's father was a doctor.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.200
My father had to sell

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.020
illegal meat

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.520
out of his ambulance in Cuba

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.560
because the government wouldn't pay him enough.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.020
I mean, Cuban doctors earn like less than 1%

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.140
than American doctors.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.620
You don't see any future,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.640
everything is stagnated.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.580
Healthcare, education,

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.580
nowadays they're in ruins.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.040
I told a Venezuelan,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.020
my Venezuelan friends, we warned you guys.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.160
Venezuela did not listen.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.040
They followed Hugo Chavez down the

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.240
socialist path.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.900
Chavez's promises impressed American celebrities too.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.260
He's a very fascinating guy.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.180
This is you and Hugo Chavez.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.480
He says, help me write my speech.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.460
Chavez said,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.560
I'll take from the rich

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.880
and give to the poor.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.460
When there was no money left,

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.320
the government just printed more.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.620
That caused inflation,

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.620
a million percent inflation.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.700
Now, a chicken costs this much.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.160
When business owners raise prices

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.900
to keep up with inflation,

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.280
government often took away their businesses.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.500
That's what's happening to this man.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.460
Chavez seized lots of private property.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.400
Chavez seized thousands and thousands of businesses

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.380
just took them away from their owners,

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.280
yet most Venezuelans

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.080
liked that.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.120
People was clapping so hard

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.980
they were like, oh finally

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.480
there's somebody here making social justice.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.640
But government grabbing private businesses

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.760
created shortages of almost everything.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.760
Why did you leave your country?

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.240
It's like the apocalypse,

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.000
it's no food,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.980
no medicine.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.380
How do you feel when you see other countries

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.060
with the same mistakes that Cuba has made

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.500
for the past decades?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.000
Terrible.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.560
Michel Ibarra escaped Cuba

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.280
and says Venezuela should

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.880
have learned from Cuba's failure.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.580
People in other countries in Latin America,

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.800
they will blame anything else besides socialism.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.940
Blaming socialism for Venezuela's riches-to-rags story

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.560
is grossly misleading.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.380
And there are plenty of socialist countries

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.880
that look nothing like Venezuela.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.220
When I talk about democratic socialism,

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.900
I'm not looking at Venezuela,

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.720
I'm not looking at Cuba.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.780
I'm looking at countries like Denmark and Sweden.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.400
Why not try my Swedish tradition?

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:13.040
Scandinavia is now called a socialist success.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.940
Even people jailed in Venezuela

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.320
like Francisco Marquez say that.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.360
I mean, you have Norway, you have Finland,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.960
you have these type of countries that are democratic

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.980
that have democratic institutions,

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.640
and many of them have socialist policies.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:26.480
In Scandinavia,

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.380
private business is largely left alone.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.160
Governments don't even set a minimum wage.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.760
Freedom rankings score Scandinavian countries

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.400
high on property rights

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.820
and business freedom.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.940
Old Danes enjoy welfare benefits.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.400
Yes, there's a big welfare state,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.480
but it's funded by thriving free enterprise.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:45.980
There we go.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:46.740
Denmark.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.640
Denmark.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.760
But so many American politicians

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.960
say Denmark is a socialist paradise,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.700
that Denmark's Prime Minister felt compelled to reply.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.920
Denmark is far from socialist

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.520
planned economy.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.180
Denmark is a market economy.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:02.980
So

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.760
if Scandinavia is not socialist,

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.320
where has socialism ever worked?

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.440
Nowhere.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.980
What would you say to the Americans

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.400
that like the idea of socialism

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.460
and support it here?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.560
I would say that they should wake up.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.420
You don't need the government to dictate

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.520
how to live your life,

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.360
how much money you should make,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.320
how your family

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.700
should be treated

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.200
or how much you should pay.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.300
If anything, I think taxes are still a bit high here.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.760
But it's the best we have in the entire world.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.040
Think about that

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.140
the next time you hear Michael Moore and celebrities

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.940
praising socialism.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.380
Socialism wrecks economies,

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.540
wrecks lives.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:45.660
And in addition,

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.260
it kills.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.660
In my next video,

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.140
I'll show you why, under socialism,

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.080
violence is inevitable.

